    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0414" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9151: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-04T18:00:00-04:00">October 4, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>970. Corson<anchor n="80" xml:id="d342-f1"/>
                    RDC Munro.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d342-f2"/>
                    Interviewed Minister Agriculture<anchor n="82" xml:id="d342-f3"/> today with
                    members Embassy present. Minister agreed: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Bolivian Government would give written approval development fund
                            obligations of RDC terminated.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Bolivian Government authorized RDC
                            deduct price premiums due from Banco Agrícola from 1945 volume
                            premiums.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Balance of available 1945 and all 1946 volume premiums to be paid to
                            producers which will help loan collections.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>RDC to ignore request to terminate
                            rubber agreement since request originated from another uninformed
                            ministry.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <pb facs="0415" n="397" xml:id="pg397"/>
                <p>Minister anxious cooperate fully RDC and
                    extremely helpful. Requests additional 250 ton export quota immediately.
                    Strongly recommend we agree since agreement will accelerate Minister’s actions
                    referred to above and will save United States money. Embassy concurs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d342-f1" n="80" xml:id="d342-f1-content">
                <p>H. G. Corson, vice president, Rubber Development Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d342-f2" n="81" xml:id="d342-f2-content">
                <p>H. H. H. Munro, representative in Bolivia of the Rubber Development
